course: dictionary
lesson: 5585
title: Linking words and groups
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A liaison is a link between two groups, so that they can talk to each other and work together. Its clues are in the sentence: «The school's parent liaison called every family about the trip.» A school needs someone to keep parents and teachers in touch, so a liaison must be a person or job that links them.
explain: Use the swap test. Put in a simpler word like link or contact, and see if the sentence still makes sense. «The school's parent link called every family about the trip» still works, so liaison means a link.
explain: The word also appears in French, where a liaison is a linking sound. In «les amis» (the friends), the silent s is said like a z, so it sounds like "lay-za-MEE". A dictionary helps when you are not sure, and it can show you more than one meaning.
fact: Liaison means the way people or groups talk to each other and work together.
fact: A liaison officer is the person whose job is to keep two groups in touch.
fact: Liaison is used in schools, the police, the army and companies, for example a parent liaison.
fact: The phrase «in liaison with» means working together with someone.
fact: In French, a liaison is a linking sound: in «les amis» the silent s is said like a z, so it sounds like "lay-za-MEE".
exercise: What does liaison mean? | A very old map | A type of food eaten at lunch | A big, loud argument | *The way two groups talk to each other and work together
exercise: «The school's parent liaison called every family about the trip.» Who is the parent liaison? | *The person who keeps the school and parents in touch | A child in the choir | A parent who teaches maths | The head teacher's dog
exercise: What is the name for linking the silent s to the next word's vowel sound in «les amis»? | Drooping | Barely | *Liaison | Famished
test: «The police officer was in liaison with the army to plan the event.» What does in liaison with mean here? | Running away from | *Working together with | Sleeping beside | Singing loudly with
test: A liaison officer keeps two groups in touch. Which job does that describe? | *A person who links two groups | A person who drives buses | A person who paints walls | A person who grows vegetables
exam: «The company hired a liaison to link its office with the factory.» What is a liaison here? | A broken machine | A type of weather | *A person or link that keeps two groups in touch | A bright light
